<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84439" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολεμ-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make hostile, make an enemy of,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>4 Ma.</u>
				4.21
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῶς οὐ πολεμώσεσθε
			αὐτούς;</span> surely <i>you will make</i> them <i>your
				enemies,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.98
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be made an enemy of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετὰ μεγίστων καιρῶν οἰκειοῦταί τε
					καὶ πολεμοῦται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.36
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπολεμώθη δὲ ὅτι . .</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				57
			</span></i>: —in other passages (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολεμουμένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.82
				</span></i>
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολεμοῦνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.20
				</span></i>
			) it is doubtful whether the word should be referred to
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολεμόω</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έω.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
